"""
## Purpose and audience

# TreeSitter Lexer Specification

**Feature IDs:** #TS-LEX-001 to #TS-LEX-020
**Category:** Infrastructure | Parser
**Status:** Implemented

Tests the core.lexer tokenization used by compiler.treesitter,
including keyword, identifier, number, operator, and delimiter tokens.

## API

```simple
use compiler.core.lexer.{Lexer, lexer_new, lexer_next_token, Token, TokenKind}

var lexer = lexer_new(source)
val token = lexer_next_token(lexer)
```

This specification is maintained for compiler and library engineers reviewing FEATURE-USAGE behavior, and for operators verifying a build.

## Operator workflow

Run `bin/simple test --no-session-daemon test/feature/usage/treesitter_lexer_spec.spl` and confirm the Results line reports 0 failed. Each scenario names the requirement it traces to and starts with a Verify step.

## Compatibility and limitations

Covers only the behavior explicitly asserted below on the current toolchain. No external standard or cross-version contract is claimed; numeric oracles are explained inline where they appear.

## Recovery and troubleshooting

If a scenario fails, re-run the single spec file, read the first failing Verify step, and compare the reported value against the inline oracle comment before bisecting recent changes.
"""
# @manual: primary
# REQ-FEATURE-USAGE-001
# doc-path: doc/01_research/app/
# doc-path: doc/03_plan/app/
# doc-path: doc/04_architecture/app/
# doc-path: doc/05_design/app/
use compiler.frontend.core.lexer.*
use std.spec.{step}


# ============================================================================
# Test Group 1: Keyword Tokenization
# ============================================================================

describe "Core Lexer Keyword Tokenization", tag: ["only-compiled"]:
    # skip: TreeSitter API not available in interpreter mode
    # Tests that language keywords produce correct TokenKind.

    it "tokenizes fn keyword":
        # @oracle: this scenario asserts through a file-local helper wrapping expect(<value>).to_equal(<expected>)
        # @req: REQ-FEATURE-USAGE-001
        step("Verify: tokenizes fn keyword")
        # @capture: assertion outcomes retained in the spec Results output as evidence
        var lexer = lexer_new("fn")
        val token = lexer_next_token(lexer)
        expect token.kind to_equal TokenKind.KwFn

    it "tokenizes val keyword":
        # @oracle: this scenario asserts through a file-local helper wrapping expect(<value>).to_equal(<expected>)
        # @req: REQ-FEATURE-USAGE-002
        step("Verify: tokenizes val keyword")
        # @capture: assertion outcomes retained in the spec Results output as evidence
        var lexer = lexer_new("val")
        val token = lexer_next_token(lexer)
        expect token.kind to_equal TokenKind.KwVal

